This licence covers the Plotwork self-hosted engine: the container image published as plotwork/selfhost and
ghcr.io/plotwork-official/plotwork-selfhost, and the files it is built from (the "Software"). It is a licence of Buun Group
Pty Ltd, a company registered in Queensland, Australia ("Plotwork", "we").

1. Free use

You may download, install, run, and copy the Software, and use it to draw diagrams, at no charge, if your use is one of these:

  a. Personal use: an individual using the Software for themselves and not on behalf of an organisation.
  b. Non-commercial use: by an individual, a registered charity or non-profit, or an educational or research institution, for
     work that is not sold and not done on behalf of a commercial organisation.
  c. Evaluation: any organisation trying the Software, for up to 30 days from its first installation, to decide whether to
     license it. Evaluation does not include use in production.
  d. Small organisations: an organisation that, together with its affiliates, has fewer than 250 employees and contractors and
     less than USD 10 million in annual revenue or funding, using the Software for its own internal work.

An "affiliate" is any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with the organisation.

2. Commercial use

Any other use by or for an organisation, including use in production by an organisation at or above either size in section
1(d), needs a commercial licence from Plotwork. The commercial licence is the self-hosting add-on to a Plotwork Enterprise
contract. Ask for one at https://plotwork.dev/enterprise. Its terms replace this licence for the organisation that holds it.

An organisation that grows past a size in section 1(d) may keep using the Software under this licence for 90 days, to obtain
a commercial licence or stop using it.

3. Conditions

  a. You may not offer the Software, or a service whose value comes mainly from it, to third parties as a hosted or managed
     service, unless a written agreement with Plotwork allows it.
  b. You may not remove or change any licence, copyright, or attribution notice in the Software, including the files under
     /licenses in the image.
  c. You may not sell, rent, or sublicense the Software. You may give a copy to someone else only with this licence, and their
     use is then under its terms.
  d. You may change the Software for your own use under section 1, but you may not distribute a changed version.

4. Third-party components

The Software contains components of other people, listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md with their licences. Those licences, not
this one, apply to those components, and nothing in this licence limits a right they give you.

5. Licence key

The Software reads a licence key from the environment variable PLOTWORK_LICENSE and reports whether one is set. It does not
stop working without one. Running it without a key does not change what this licence allows.

